-          "quote": "Input an integer $k\\ge1$, a strictly increasing finite grid $t_0<\\cdots<t_N$ with $N\\ge k$, starting states $Y_0,\\ldots,Y_{k-1}\\in\\mathbb R^d$, and a vector field $f$ defined at every requested evaluation. On a dimension mismatch or a grid with repeated or decreasing nodes, return `invalid-input` or `invalid-grid`. Evaluate and store $F_j=f(t_j,Y_j)$ for $j=0,\\ldots,k-1$; an undefined evaluation returns `evaluation-failure` with the valid prefix.\n\nFor $n=k-1,\\ldots,N-1$, construct the predictor weights $b_j^n$ and corrector weights $\\widehat b_j^n$ from the actual nodes as in [[lem-variable-step-adams-lagrange-weights]], then do the following:\n\n1. Predict $Y_{n+1}^P=Y_n+\\sum_{j=0}^{k-1}b_j^nF_{n-j}$.\n2. Evaluate $F_{n+1}^P=f(t_{n+1},Y_{n+1}^P)$. If undefined, return `evaluation-failure` with phase `predictor`.\n3. Correct once by setting $Y_{n+1}=Y_n+\\widehat b_0^nF_{n+1}^P+\\sum_{j=1}^{k}\\widehat b_j^nF_{n+1-j}$.\n4. Evaluate and store $F_{n+1}=f(t_{n+1},Y_{n+1})$ for the next predictor. If undefined, return `evaluation-failure` with phase `post-corrector` and the computed $Y_{n+1}$.\n\nAfter all steps return `completed` with the states. This is one predictor and one corrector pass; it does not solve the fully implicit Adams corrector equation and asserts no convergence, stability, or error bound.",
+          "quote": "Input an integer $k\\ge1$, a finite grid $t_0,\\ldots,t_N$ with $N\\ge k$, starting states $Y_0,\\ldots,Y_{k-1}\\in\\mathbb R^d$, and a vector field $f:U\\to\\mathbb R^d$ on its evaluation domain $U$. Before evaluating $f$, if any starting state has dimension different from $d$, return `invalid-input`; otherwise, if the grid is not strictly increasing, return `invalid-grid`. Evaluate and store $F_j=f(t_j,Y_j)$ for $j=0,\\ldots,k-1$; an undefined evaluation outside $U$ returns `evaluation-failure` with the valid prefix.\n\nFor $n=k-1,\\ldots,N-1$, construct the predictor weights $b_j^n$ and corrector weights $\\widehat b_j^n$ from the actual nodes as in [[lem-variable-step-adams-lagrange-weights]], then do the following:\n\n1. Predict $Y_{n+1}^P=Y_n+\\sum_{j=0}^{k-1}b_j^nF_{n-j}$.\n2. Evaluate $F_{n+1}^P=f(t_{n+1},Y_{n+1}^P)$. If undefined, return `evaluation-failure` with phase `predictor`.\n3. Correct once by setting $Y_{n+1}=Y_n+\\widehat b_0^nF_{n+1}^P+\\sum_{j=1}^{k}\\widehat b_j^nF_{n+1-j}$.\n4. Evaluate and store $F_{n+1}=f(t_{n+1},Y_{n+1})$ for the next predictor. If undefined, return `evaluation-failure` with phase `post-corrector` and the computed $Y_{n+1}$.\n\nAfter all steps return `completed` with the states. This is one predictor and one corrector pass; it does not solve the fully implicit Adams corrector equation and asserts no convergence, stability, or error bound.",
